                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "noddy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb7dc7e2-fb16-3632-af60-0e5636a31162",
                                        "entry_id": "ed03a89e-0857-311c-b0f7-3a067dadba29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A silly or stupid person; a fool, an idiot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12e59722-16cf-4c49-be9c-b79e3fac7fc8",
                                                "sense_id": "eb7dc7e2-fb16-3632-af60-0e5636a31162",
                                                "text": "I graunt for my parte by fayth of my body / why where the deuyll is this horeſon nody"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be55f3c5-bf37-44a8-b1fa-1ed53cf1a9fb",
                                                "sense_id": "eb7dc7e2-fb16-3632-af60-0e5636a31162",
                                                "text": "Hum[phrey]. If it be ſo, my friend, you vſe me fine, / VVhat do you thinke I am? / Iasp[er]. An arrant noddie / Hum. A vvord of obliquie, novv by Gods bodie, / I'le tell thy maiſter for I knovv thee vvell."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a6b46f3-f983-4003-8159-a074fd4108ee",
                                                "sense_id": "eb7dc7e2-fb16-3632-af60-0e5636a31162",
                                                "text": "Leo Decimus [Pope Leo X] that ſcoffing Pope, […] took an extraordinary delight in humoring of ſilly fellovves, and to put gulleries vpon them, […] he made ſoft fellovves ſtarke noddies, and ſuch as vvere fooliſh, quite mad before hee left them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32edba61-e8eb-41d8-b278-1d454fc89704",
                                                "sense_id": "eb7dc7e2-fb16-3632-af60-0e5636a31162",
                                                "text": "VVere not Thoſe bleſſed days vvhen our Divines had Saleſmen, and Mechaniques for their Tryers; and the Laity a ſupercilious Company of Claſſical, and Congregational Noddys for the Inſpectours of our Lives and Manners: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ce69c5f-b5cc-4c7f-aab6-3b18731e9f22",
                                                "sense_id": "eb7dc7e2-fb16-3632-af60-0e5636a31162",
                                                "text": "VVhy, vvhat a noddy have I been, to take this ſtrapper alvvays for a girl!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e80d055b-85cd-4a05-97b0-a1551463a0fb",
                                                "sense_id": "eb7dc7e2-fb16-3632-af60-0e5636a31162",
                                                "text": "[T]hough I am but a simple noddy, / I think one Shakespear [William Shakespeare] puts the same thought in / The mouth of some one in his plays so doating, / Which many people pass for wits by quoting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51408080-f87e-447a-aff2-17a5fca56ef8",
                                                "sense_id": "eb7dc7e2-fb16-3632-af60-0e5636a31162",
                                                "text": "At last the people in a body / To the Town Hall came flocking: / \"'Tis clear,\" cried they, \"our Mayor's a noddy; / And as for our Corporation—shocking[…]\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5987f23b-9f56-3309-9262-8dbe986a4c1e",
                                        "entry_id": "ed03a89e-0857-311c-b0f7-3a067dadba29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In full knave noddy: the jack or knave playing card."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b98267d-6cf6-4cd4-832d-e4e269815736",
                                                "sense_id": "5987f23b-9f56-3309-9262-8dbe986a4c1e",
                                                "text": "The ſpout of ſport, and follies turtle Doue, / Noddie turn'd vp, all made, yet loſe the tricke."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10196fac-37f5-4db4-9c5b-1a9ac5ec8ae0",
                                                "sense_id": "5987f23b-9f56-3309-9262-8dbe986a4c1e",
                                                "text": "You vvant four, and I tvvo, and my Deal: Novv, Knave noddy—no, Hearts be Trumps."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "622128be-a070-38ca-bc6a-9caa5ec05e39",
                                        "entry_id": "ed03a89e-0857-311c-b0f7-3a067dadba29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In full noddy-fifteen: a certain card game related to cribbage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "238a6fd9-9f80-4b69-b54c-d37600e42bc1",
                                                "sense_id": "622128be-a070-38ca-bc6a-9caa5ec05e39",
                                                "text": "[W]ell let not me take you at Noddy anie more, leaſt I preſent you to the pariſh for a gamſter, this is the ninth ſet that you haue loſt, and yet you will not leaue off."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8753de7a-11fa-4568-8052-68afe35d10f3",
                                                "sense_id": "622128be-a070-38ca-bc6a-9caa5ec05e39",
                                                "text": "Let 'hem embrace more frugal pastimes. VVhy ſhould not the thriftie and right vvorſhipfull game of Poſt and payre content 'hem? Or the vvittie inuention of Noddie, for counters? or God make them rich, at the Tables? but Masking, and Reuelling?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8096c707-baff-43ee-a80f-a6cfa01ac2f5",
                                                "sense_id": "622128be-a070-38ca-bc6a-9caa5ec05e39",
                                                "text": "[H]e told me he had him at command when he was a page, but by plaieing to [too] much at primeroe and noddy he loſt Time and his monie to [too]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c95a8d0b-25ca-43e9-b14d-74cd6ecfeaec",
                                                "sense_id": "622128be-a070-38ca-bc6a-9caa5ec05e39",
                                                "text": "An old game of cards, conjectured to be the same as cribbage. […] Noddy is now played as follows: Any number can play—the cards are all dealt out—the elder hand plays one, (of which he hath a pair or a prial if a good player)—saying or singing \"there's a good card for thee,\" passing it to his right hand neighbour—the person next in succession who holds its pair covers it, saying \"there's still a better than he;\" and passes both onward—the person holding the third of the sort (ace, six, queen, or what not) puts it on with \"there's the best of all three:\" and the holder of the fourth crowns all with the emphatic—\"And there is Niddy-Noddeee.\"—He wins the tack, turns it down, and begins again. He who is first out receives from his adversaries a fish (or a bean, as the case may be) for each unplayed card."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "912fb824-49b2-30c6-941b-c70e7d45b938",
                                        "entry_id": "ed03a89e-0857-311c-b0f7-3a067dadba29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In full noddy-fifteen: a certain card game related to cribbage.",
                                            "Synonym of sexual intercourse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "historical",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3c7d8ed-c61e-4576-bb46-25f3c560fb3a",
                                                "sense_id": "912fb824-49b2-30c6-941b-c70e7d45b938",
                                                "text": "I left her at Cardes, ſhee'll ſit vp till you come, becauſe ſhee'll haue you play a game at Noddie; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "noddy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db45dab7-0673-3a03-9100-a94047b0c39e",
                                        "entry_id": "315d2e7a-b79f-3fb7-b9f1-e02b9dbdfe55",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Foolish, silly, stupid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "England",
                                            "regional"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbeb7045-cb88-4f8b-b031-d6e4e27e2266",
                                                "sense_id": "db45dab7-0673-3a03-9100-a94047b0c39e",
                                                "text": "For that no man shulde se / Nor rede in any scrolles / Of theyr dronken nolles, / Nor of theyr noddy polles, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7b3559d-d1ea-4114-8fca-386beff64d10",
                                                "sense_id": "db45dab7-0673-3a03-9100-a94047b0c39e",
                                                "text": "I beſeech you, VVill your VViſdoms, or common Senſe, or Underſtanding, or vvhat you vvill call it, approve of nothing in our Common-Prayer Book, that you preſent us vvith an inane nihil, a nevv Directory of a noddy Synod, or find you ſo many Deficiencies in Monarchical Government, that you ſhould ſeek to introduce an Ochlocracy, a People Svvay?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "noddy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36ddcfcd-5ef4-3ffb-866f-9245fcfcce59",
                                        "entry_id": "18698b1c-767a-344f-9f85-409821ee8793",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of noddify (“to make (someone) into a noddy (noun sense 1), to make a fool of”)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0fea7d0-6b17-45fc-a98e-7f6e6ddeb375",
                                                "sense_id": "36ddcfcd-5ef4-3ffb-866f-9245fcfcce59",
                                                "text": "If ſuch an Aſſe be noddied for the nonce, / I ſay but this, to helpe his Idle fit; / Let him but thanke himſelfe for lacke of VVit, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "noddy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04285676-f077-3eaf-8d95-aff7fee45910",
                                        "entry_id": "aa608ae3-5cf5-3c1f-b4de-019e29325e2f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several stout-bodied, gregarious terns of the genus Anous found in tropical seas, especially the brown noddy or common noddy (Anous stolidus)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be7e35d3-8de4-4d74-a117-95990d829d94",
                                                "sense_id": "04285676-f077-3eaf-8d95-aff7fee45910",
                                                "text": "VVe savv no Land this Day, but ſavv a great many Snakes and ſome VVhales. VVe ſavv alſo ſome Boobies, and Noddy-birds; and in the Night caught one of theſe laſt. […] The Top or Crovvn of the Head of this Noddy was Coal-black, having alſo ſmall black Streaks round about and cloſe to the Eyes; and round theſe Streaks on each ſide, a pretty broad vvhite Circle. The Breaſt, Belly, and under part of the VVings of this Noddy vvere vvhite: And the Back and upper part of its VVings of a faint black or ſmoak Colour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d865ada3-8c90-48a9-9fdc-52df2af6505b",
                                                "sense_id": "04285676-f077-3eaf-8d95-aff7fee45910",
                                                "text": "The Rocks and outer Lines of the Iſland, are the Haunts of variety of Sea-Birds, eſpecially Boobies and Noddies; […] The Noddies are ſmaller and flat footed alſo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c46dbd43-1c26-4914-bf98-0d425f66e2df",
                                                "sense_id": "04285676-f077-3eaf-8d95-aff7fee45910",
                                                "text": "At noon ſome noddies came ſo near to us, that one of them was caught by hand. This bird was about the ſize of a ſmall pigeon. I divided it, vvith its entrails, into 18 portions, and by a vvell-knovvn method at ſea, of, VVho ſhall have this? it vvas diſtributed, vvith the allovvance of bread and vvater for dinner, and eat up bones and all, vvith ſalt vvater for ſauce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11cc5b06-d32a-4c59-a483-3a352dc41abc",
                                                "sense_id": "04285676-f077-3eaf-8d95-aff7fee45910",
                                                "text": "At length they caught two boobies, and a noddy, / And then they left off eating the dead body."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57e43749-7ae1-4c35-9b06-ce696bf23f39",
                                                "sense_id": "04285676-f077-3eaf-8d95-aff7fee45910",
                                                "text": "We only observed two kinds of birds [on Saint Peter and Saint Paul Archipelago]—the booby and the noddy. The former is a species of gannet, and the latter a tern. Both are of a tame and stupid disposition, and are so unaccustomed to visiters,^([sic – meaning visitors]) that I could have killed any number of them with my geological hammer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dc16f26-1629-4f21-b7a1-4ef99c36a245",
                                                "sense_id": "04285676-f077-3eaf-8d95-aff7fee45910",
                                                "text": "A cloud of sea birds hovered overhead, the gannets diving with folded wings, while the black noddy-terns fluttered down in companies each time the fish drove the small fry to the surface."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "118d3fc7-248f-39c3-a54c-1a737f708cc8",
                                        "entry_id": "aa608ae3-5cf5-3c1f-b4de-019e29325e2f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small two-wheeled carriage drawn by a single horse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8036a4c-a11a-46c0-b024-9a9c7435556f",
                                                "sense_id": "118d3fc7-248f-39c3-a54c-1a737f708cc8",
                                                "text": "[S]he has brought over a nevv language vvith her. […] VVhy a new kind of a London Engliſh, that's no more like our Iriſh Engliſh, than a coxcomb's fine gilded chariot like a Glaſſmanogue [i.e., Phibsborough, Dublin] noddy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58f0439f-bc3b-48de-b757-3bffe9abc344",
                                                "sense_id": "118d3fc7-248f-39c3-a54c-1a737f708cc8",
                                                "text": "\"By Jove, I think one of us must go into town.[…]\" / \"Let's see Nutter—you or I must go—we'll take one of these songster's \"noddies.\"[\"] [A \"noddy,\" give me leave to remark, was the one-horse hack vehicle of Dublin and the country round, which has since given place to the jaunting car, which is, in turn, half superseded by the cab.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3716c1b2-b537-40af-a8c8-655c27ffdd56",
                                                "sense_id": "118d3fc7-248f-39c3-a54c-1a737f708cc8",
                                                "text": "Down there Emmet was hanged, drawn and quartered. Greasy black rope. Dogs licking the blood off the street when the lord lieutenant's wife drove by in her noddy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60e4f669-6b4a-31c3-9ed8-95287c5e5af1",
                                        "entry_id": "aa608ae3-5cf5-3c1f-b4de-019e29325e2f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of fellatio."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Multicultural-London-English",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c2167c9-a198-48af-8fec-e3ad1d277357",
                                                "sense_id": "60e4f669-6b4a-31c3-9ed8-95287c5e5af1",
                                                "text": "Bakin' off of this light skin hottie / Sweet ting, arch ya up and give noddy"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2794292-34ab-3483-acb2-c1eb107e4b7b",
                                        "entry_id": "aa608ae3-5cf5-3c1f-b4de-019e29325e2f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of northern fulmar (“an Arctic seabird, Fulmarus glacialis”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Newfoundland",
